# ── the stock: the archived migration tree, kept on disk as reference material ──────────────
# Mined by hand for CONTENT (what is true: conventions, formulas, edge cases, oracles), never
# for STRUCTURE. Never imported by the library. Gitignored because it is not this project's
# code and must never be mistaken for it; its pushed backup is the archived
# `pricebook-migration` repo (tag `migration-archive`).
_stock/

# ── the prompt channel (Code <-> Cowork) — local working state, not repo content ────────────
.cowork/thread.md
# Orphaned copies the editing surface leaves behind when it rewrites an open file on a FUSE
# mount. They are stale snapshots of the thread, and one showed up untracked after the first
# exchange — ignored so a stale copy of the channel can never be committed by accident.
.fuse_hidden*

# ── macOS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Held source material — PDFs of books and papers we work from. Never committed: this repo is
# PUBLIC, and the sources are copyrighted. `docs/references.md` records WHAT is held and its
# status; the file itself stays local, exactly as the BERHAN thesis does under `_stock/`.
docs/papers/*.pdf
docs/papers/*.djvu
docs/papers/*.epub

# ── the Substack journal & drafts — local working state, not repo content ───────────────────
# The narrative/dev-journal behind the Substack series (FP-1 in docs/future_projects.md). Kept
# OUT of the tracked tree: this repo is PUBLIC, and the series is a separate downstream project
# (a consumer of the library), not the analytics library itself. docs/future_projects.md records
# THAT it exists and where; the files themselves stay local, exactly as _stock/ and
# .cowork/thread.md do.
_substack/
